      "payload": "{\"messages\":[{\"content\":\"<customer id=\\\"customer:c_1003\\\">\\nCustomer Priya Nair (c_1003), member, country UK.\\n</customer>\\n<ticket id=\\\"order:o_7815\\\">\\nOrder o_7815 placed 2026-09-29, standard shipping, status delivered, delivered 2026-10-01T09:30:00Z. Items: Winter gloves, S (39.00).\\n</ticket>\\n<ticket id=\\\"ticket:t_5003\\\">\\nTicket t_5003 for order o_7815: stage open, routed as returns, return requested False, label sent False, refund none, attempts 0.\\n</ticket>\\n<crm_note id=\\\"crm:c_1003:0001\\\">\\nChat with Priya Nair, prior to the current order. Customer asked whether she would be charged import duties on delivery to the UK, having had a bad experience with another retailer. Agent confirmed that for UK orders duties and taxes are included at checkout and nothing is payable on delivery. Customer thanked the agent and said she would order gloves for the winter.\\n</crm_note>\\n<policy id=\\\"kb:refunds-and-exchanges@4#1\\\">\\nTo exchange a size or colour, start a return for the original and place a new order; the new order ships immediately and the return is refunded when it arrives. Exchanges are not held in stock.\\n</policy>\\n<policy id=\\\"kb:refunds-and-exchanges@4#3\\\">\\nShipping charges are refunded only when the return is our fault: a damaged, defective or wrong item.\\n</policy>\\n<policy id=\\\"kb:returns-policy@5#1\\\">\\nFinal-sale items, gift cards and personalised products cannot be returned. Footwear can be returned if it has only been tried on indoors.\\n</policy>\\n<policy id=\\\"kb:returns-policy@5#2\\\">\\nTo start a return, open the order in your account and choose Return items. We email a prepaid label within minutes; drop the parcel at any carrier point within 14 days of requesting the return.\\n</policy>\\n<format id=\\\"contract:json-reply\\\">\\nReply as JSON with exactly these keys: \\\"reply\\\" (the message to the customer, at most 120 words, plain text), \\\"next_stage\\\" (one of: open, awaiting_photos, return_requested, label_sent, refund_pending, resolved, needs_agent), \\\"citations\\\" (the list of policy article ids you relied on). No other keys, no text outside the JSON.\\n</format>\\n<message id=\\\"turn:s_c2_06:0001\\\">\\nCan I return the gloves if they're the wrong size?\\n</message>\\n\",\"role\":\"user\"}],\"system\":[{\"id\":\"policy:returns\",\"text\":\"You are the Northwind Outdoors support assistant, handling a return or refund request. Use only the customer and ticket facts, the CRM notes, the policy articles and the conversation you are given.\\n\\nExplain what the customer can do next in plain steps, cite the policy article id for every rule you state, and never promise a refund amount or date the articles do not state.\\n\\nNever include the customer's phone number, email address, postal address or any payment detail in your reply, and never mention another customer or another order than the one on this ticket.\\n\\nSet next_stage to return_requested when the customer asks to return or exchange and the policy allows it, to refund_pending when the item is already on its way back, and to open when you need more from the customer; use needs_agent only when the articles do not cover the request.\"}],\"tools\":[]}"
